11
00:00:16,577 --> 00:00:18,917
We don't. Until today's announcement.

12
00:00:19,343 --> 00:00:21,623
Experts say hiding pay makes it easier to

13
00:00:21,523 --> 00:00:23,857
offer lower wages... ...especially to young

14
00:00:23,757 --> 00:00:25,616
people and women entering the workforce.

15
00:00:26,043 --> 00:00:27,843
Anyone who has searched for a job knows

16
00:00:27,743 --> 00:00:28,523
that frustration.

17
00:00:28,878 --> 00:00:31,278
So what changed? Did they finally run out

18
00:00:31,178 --> 00:00:31,718
of excuses?

19
00:00:32,005 --> 00:00:34,505
Not quite. They just ran into a new rule.

20
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:36,340
A rule? Or another committee meeting?

21
00:00:36,759 --> 00:00:38,759
Prime Minister Andy Burnham announced a

22
00:00:38,659 --> 00:00:39,380
bold shift.

23
00:00:39,686 --> 00:00:41,766
Prime Minister Andy Burnham says whether

24
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:43,486
you're starting out or supporting a family,

25
00:00:43,846 --> 00:00:45,206
you should know what a job pays.

26
00:00:45,452 --> 00:00:47,512
You should know what a job pays before applying?

27
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:49,411
The government plans to make it a legal

28
00:00:49,311 --> 00:00:49,891
requirement.

29
00:00:50,022 --> 00:00:52,462
Wait—does this apply to every single vacancy?

30
00:00:53,036 --> 00:00:55,376
Early analysis shows overwhelming backing

31
00:00:55,276 --> 00:00:57,820
for the plan. Nearly all responding businesses

32
00:00:57,720 --> 00:01:00,100
agreed transparency is necessary.

33
00:01:00,596 --> 00:01:02,376
The government says the goal is to break

34
00:01:02,276 --> 00:01:03,896
down barriers for job seekers.

35
00:01:04,133 --> 00:01:06,193
But what exactly must we publish? A fixed

36
00:01:06,093 --> 00:01:07,233
amount or range?

37
00:01:07,655 --> 00:01:10,255
Ministers haven't decided that yet. Or the

38
00:01:10,155 --> 00:01:10,555
penalties.

39
00:01:10,944 --> 00:01:13,044
So we are flying blind on how to comply?

40
00:01:13,496 --> 00:01:15,816
The promise is clear, but the fine print

41
00:01:15,716 --> 00:01:16,456
remains murky.

42
00:01:16,789 --> 00:01:19,189
This move aims to fix 'salary blindness'

43
00:01:19,089 --> 00:01:19,889
for applicants.

44
00:01:20,263 --> 00:01:22,883
Does it guarantee equal pay? Or just equal

45
00:01:22,783 --> 00:01:23,143
guessing?

46
00:01:23,514 --> 00:01:25,514
It will not magically erase discrimination

47
00:01:25,414 --> 00:01:26,634
overnight, but it helps!

48
00:01:26,963 --> 00:01:29,363
Fair enough. At least we can finally compare

49
00:01:29,263 --> 00:01:29,723
our bills.

50
00:01:30,139 --> 00:01:32,379
The policy also targets a massive youth

51
00:01:32,279 --> 00:01:33,079
employment gap.

52
00:01:33,366 --> 00:01:35,666
Nearly one million young adults are currently

53
00:01:35,566 --> 00:01:37,046
inactive or unemployed.

54
00:01:37,384 --> 00:01:39,064
So the government wants them to actually

55
00:01:38,964 --> 00:01:39,744
apply now?

56
00:01:40,038 --> 00:01:42,458
Yes! Plus, they are hunting for two hundred

57
00:01:42,358 --> 00:01:43,518
thousand placements...

58
00:01:43,608 --> 00:01:46,428
For teens? Wait—doesn't that sound like

59
00:01:46,328 --> 00:01:47,068
a summer camp?

60
00:01:47,349 --> 00:01:49,389
Companies like Siemens have pledged ten

61
00:01:49,289 --> 00:01:51,666
thousand engineering spots. But the full

62
00:01:51,566 --> 00:01:54,006
Milburn Review on youth inactivity is pending.

63
00:01:54,409 --> 00:01:56,469
So what happens if a company just ignores

64
00:01:56,369 --> 00:01:56,969
